{"boundary":"This is static tracked source text. Use it for source grounding only; do not infer private runtime state from it.","chunkCount":81,"chunkHash":"4ea31d7e38a6061a6327192f6c301d7fadf0ad839fe10a1d37a5a28fb44c0d76","chunkIndex":5,"chunkText":"Frozen evaluation retains the shipped/default non-Fleet repetition penalty of `1.1`, while Fleet qualification uses the neutral value `1.0` because its canonical event graphs must copy the exact scenario ID 11–22 times. The agent-bound value is recorded in independently verified generation evidence; no operator override is accepted. This Fleet-specific offline qualification setting is not an iOS or device-validation claim. The evaluator rejects duplicate JSON object keys and treats any Cortex `rejectedToolID` or `rejectedToolIDs` catalog as a retry-eligible contract failure. Every one of the 504 Cortex cases also carries a critical record-aware offline route metric: actionable cases require an exact persisted action bound to the selected manifest tool, clarification cases require the exact missing arguments and a question with no action, contrast cases require the compact five-field selection shape, and no-tool or invalid-tool cases require their exact null-selection state. Those five-field and `actionStep` shapes qualify the adapter; they do not replace the shipped iOS `action`/`final` wire schema. Candidate JSONL evidence is loaded with the same unique-key policy. Replaying the old adapter with repetition penalty `1.1` made two prior runaway cases syntactically bounded but did not repair their semantics, while the second trigger-list case still failed strict JSON after one retry; only a fresh retrain and unchanged held-out expectations can establish behavioral recovery.

Prelaunch local validation passed after these corrections: 341 Unsloth tests passed with two pinned-environment integration tests skipped, including all 91 adapter-evaluation tests; the focused 145-test Cortex/dataset/Fleet quality selection passed; and the prescribed non-slow/non-E2E crawler suite passed all 492 selected tests with 125 deselected. Python compilation, launcher shell syntax, and `git diff --check` also passed. `uv` is unavailable on this Ubuntu host, so the equivalent `python3 -m pytest` collection and execution paths were used and no `uv.lock` byproduct was created. These checks validate source and deterministic corpus contracts; they do not replace the pending fresh model-backed run.
